 ### Windows (PowerShell)
-Double-click `start.bat` or run:
+From the repository folder, run:
 ```powershell
-powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\serve.ps1
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\server.ps1
+```
+
+Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/ in your browser. The server uses its script directory,
+so it can also be launched from another working directory. Use `-Port 8081` to
+choose a different port.
+
+### GitHub Pages
+In repository **Settings → Pages**, choose **Deploy from a branch**, select
+`main` and `/ (root)`, and save. Repository admin access is required to enable
+Pages. The lowercase `index.html` is the homepage; no build command is needed.
+
+### Tests
+With the local server running, open http://127.0.0.1:8080/tests.html. The page
+runs the browser test suite and reports its assertions and failure count.
 
